# .gitignore — BramaOS
#
# Rules for editing this file:
#   1. Every entry belongs under one of the commented sections below. If a new
#      entry fits none of them, add a new section with a one-line rationale.
#   2. Ignore by pattern, not by instance. Add `*.log`, not `debug-2026-09-15.log`.
#   3. Never ignore a file to hide a problem. Generated junk in the working dir
#      means a tool is misconfigured — fix the tool, then ignore its output.
#   4. Committed-by-design files are listed under "Explicitly tracked" at the
#      bottom with `!` negations. Do not remove them without a matching change
#      to docs/product-description.md.
#   5. Secrets are never committed, never force-added. If a secret lands in a
#      commit, rotate it — removing it from history is not enough.

# --- Go build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# Single static binary, built from cmd/brama. Name matches the CLI binary.
/brama
/brama.exe
/dist/
/build/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# --- Go test & tooling artifacts ---------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# --- Brama runtime state -----------------------------------------------------
# .brama/ is server-side deployment state (state.json, backups/). It is created
# on deploy targets, never in this repo — ignored so local end-to-end runs
# against a loopback target can't leak a host's history into git.
.brama/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Brama holds no secret custody: SSH identity lives in ssh-agent / ~/.ssh, and
# per-environment secrets live in shared/.env on the target. Nothing below
# should ever exist here; these patterns are a backstop, not a workflow.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519
!*.pub

# --- Local scratch & fixtures ------------------------------------------------
# .scratch/ is agent working space (see docs/agents/). tmp/ is ad-hoc.
.scratch/
tmp/
*.local
*.local.*

# --- Learning workspace ------------------------------------------------------
# learn/ is a personal Go teaching workspace (lessons, references, progress).
# It is about the author, not the product, and carries no build or runtime role.
learn/

# --- Editors & IDEs ----------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Explicitly tracked ------------------------------------------------------
# brama.yaml is project config and is committed by design — it declares intent
# (branches, targets, policies), it does not carry credentials.
!brama.yaml
